# Gameplay reproduction for inc-p0h1 (Bestow Curse redesign), the PLAYER
# MENU code path this bead adds -- only reachable on the branch build --
# picking the THIRD of its three curses: a hesitation that costs the victim
# roughly half its actions. Sibling of
# tools/keys/bestow-curse-menu-ability.keys; see that file's header for the
# general wizard-mode setup.
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/bestow-curse-menu-hesitation.keys 1
#
# NOT Frozen, on purpose: the hesitation roll only happens inside a
# monster's own turn (src/Monster.cpp:366, "if (HasStati(HESITATION))"), so
# a frozen goblin -- one that never takes a turn at all -- would never roll
# it and the message would never print. The goblin is left free to act (and
# to fight back), and the player spends several turns waiting ('.', Wait One
# Turn) in place so time passes for it to keep trying -- 's' (Search) will
# not do this: it cancels itself the instant a hostile is in view ("You
# stop searching (hostile to goblin)."), spending no game time at all, as
# measured on this exact scenario.
#
# "The <goblin> hesitates, unable to act." (src/Monster.cpp:378, IDPrint,
# not the victim's own IPrint) is a THIRD-PERSON message shown to any
# player who perceives the hesitating creature, printed at most once per
# game tick (Status.Val guards it) with roughly even odds (random(2)) each
# time the goblin's turn comes up -- so across several of the player's own
# turns it should repeat, interleaved with the goblin's own attacks on the
# turns it does NOT hesitate.

@include chargen-priest.keys
ESC

w
y
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Bestow Curse"
ENTER

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Goblinkin"
@choose "goblin"
RIGHT ENTER
@dump:goblin-summoned

m
@choose "Bestow Curse"
RIGHT
ENTER
@dump:curse-menu

@choose "a hesitation that claims half its actions"
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:cast-hesitation

.
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:tick-1
.
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:tick-2
.
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:tick-3
.
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:tick-4
.
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:tick-5
.
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:tick-6
.
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:tick-7
.
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:tick-8

v
DOWN*40
@dump:message-log
@while "Messages" ESC

@quit
